FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/runtime.rs:2719-2726 — The new `first_invalid_base64_padding` has sub-branches with no test on either side: the `% 4 == 1` refusal ("A===", "AAAAA===", "AAAAA=") at line 2721, and the `required == 2` excess-padding arm (e.g. "AA===") at line 2726. Every test added this round hits only `first_pad % 4` of 0, 2 or 3, or the "followed by data" arm; `grep` of `tests/encoding_hashing_test.rs` shows no input whose first pad sits at index 1 mod 4. The phase's own edge matrix claims malformed base64 is "covered", but two newly added refusal paths are unreachable by any test, so a regression that removed them would still pass. Fix: add `base64.decode("A===")`, `base64.decode("AAAAA===")` and `base64.decode("AA===")` cases with the expected positions (1, 5, 4). — VERIFIED: read the full branch at src/runtime.rs:2712-2732 and the complete test list at tests/encoding_hashing_test.rs:289-377; no case has `first_pad % 4 == 1`.

2. [MINOR] tests/encoding_hashing_test.rs:248-254 — SPEC.md promises `uuid.generate()` answers a "random version-4 UUID", but the test asserts only parse-round-trip, length 36, and that two draws differ. A UUID with version nibble 0/1/3 and variant bits from raw random bytes would satisfy every assertion. Fix: assert the 15th hex character is `4` and the 20th is one of `8`/`9`/`a`/`b` (RFC 4122 variant), or compare against `uuid::Uuid::parse_str(id).get_version_num() == 4` in the Rust harness.

3. [MINOR] tests/encoding_hashing_test.rs:262-275 — SPEC.md says `uuid.parse` accepts the hyphenated, simple, braced and `urn:uuid:` forms "in either case", but the test exercises only lowercase forms (lowercase `urn:uuid:` prefix, lowercase simple/braced bodies) with uppercase *hex digits* in the hyphenated case. If the crate ever treated the `urn:uuid:` prefix case-sensitively, or braced/simple uppercase was mishandled, the documented guarantee would silently regress. Fix: add `URN:UUID:550E8400-E29B-41D4-A716-446655440000` and `{550E8400-E29B-41D4-A716-446655440000}` to the loop.

4. [MINOR] src/runtime.rs:4133-4141 — The `uuid.parse` non-text argument refusal is untested, and neither is the documented text-input form of `hex.encode`/`base64.encode` (`bytes_argument`'s `Value::Text` branch at src/runtime.rs:2615 is only ever reached through `hash.*`). tests/encoding_hashing_test.rs:381-396 covers `hash.sha256(5)`, `hex.encode(5)`, `hex.encode([256])`, `base64.encode([-1])`, and malformed text for `uuid.parse`, but no `uuid.parse(5)` and no `hex.encode("hi")` / `base64.encode("hi")` despite SPEC.md saying both encoders accept text. The edge matrix's `type_mismatch` row is therefore overstated for the UUID module. Fix: add `uuid.parse(5)` to the name-check table and one text-input encoder assertion each.

